codex
The fixed `If` semantics encodes branch selection through a concrete `#branch(true|false)` constructor, so it cannot symbolically split on an unknown character code. That is a genuine modeling limitation for this syntax, not a reason to bypass execution. I’m repairing the program within the same accepted subset by expressing the one-shot conditional as a terminating inner `while`; the supplied `while` rules branch by guarded conditions and therefore remain symbolically executable.
apply patch
